Arcade bar: one vblank of the machine per retro_run.

Upstream Flycast (single-threaded) stops the SH4 when the game presents a frame, or after a render
timeout (50 ms of guest time; the fork made it 25 ms); retro_run then lasts as long as the game
takes to draw, two vblanks for a 30 fps game, three at a scene change. The bar's worker calls
retro_run at the fps the core reports and its netplay counts frames: guest time per call must be
constant. So the SH4 stops at every vblank (Emulator::vblank, at the end of that timeslice) and
never when a frame is presented (Renderer_if.cpp); a vblank without a new frame is a duplicate.
Stops always fall on the same guest cycles, so where a frame ends is the same on every machine.

diff --git a/core/emulator.cpp b/core/emulator.cpp
--- a/core/emulator.cpp
+++ b/core/emulator.cpp
@@ -1078,24 +1078,18 @@
 {
 	EventManager::event(Event::VBlank);
 	runner.execTasks();
-	// Time out if a frame hasn't been rendered for 50 ms
 #ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
-	// ★ PACER-SPREAD (2026-07-24): stop a render-less run at the SECOND vblank
-	// (~33ms guest), not the third (50ms). Transitions skip ~3 vblanks without
-	// presenting; at the upstream threshold one emu.render() gulps 50ms of
-	// guest time inside a single host frame (the [SPIKE2] guest_ms=50.0
-	// signature) and the wall cost lands as a 60-220ms hitch. Returning the
-	// host frame earlier lets unpaid debt carry in fly_owed and drain across
-	// the next ticks as brief slowmo instead of a freeze. Threshold grid is
-	// discrete (check runs only at vblanks): <=1.5 vblanks selects stop-at-#2.
-	// 30fps-native titles present from the vblank-#2 ISR, which runs AFTER
-	// this callback — they now dupe at #2 and present at the top of the next
-	// tick; JGR feel-check is the eyes gate for that.
-	const u64 fly_render_timeout_cycles = 5000000;
-#else
-	const u64 fly_render_timeout_cycles = 10000000;
+	// Arcade bar (flycast/patches/0002): every retro_run emulates exactly one vblank, so the
+	// frontend's frame is the machine's and its pacing, input delay and rollback all count in
+	// the same frames. The SH4 stops here (at the end of this timeslice), never when the game
+	// presents a frame (Renderer_if.cpp) nor after a render timeout: guest time per call is
+	// constant, whatever the game draws.
+	if (!config::ThreadedRendering)
+		getSh4Executor()->Stop();
+	return;
 #endif
-	if (sh4_sched_now64() - startTime <= fly_render_timeout_cycles)
+	// Time out if a frame hasn't been rendered for 50 ms
+	if (sh4_sched_now64() - startTime <= 10000000)
 		return;
 	renderTimeout = true;
 	if (ggpo::active())
diff --git a/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp b/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp
--- a/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp
+++ b/core/hw/pvr/Renderer_if.cpp
@@ -270,8 +270,10 @@
 #endif
 		{
 			presented = true;
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__	// arcade bar: the SH4 stops at each vblank instead (emulator.cpp)
 			if (!config::ThreadedRendering && !ggpo::active())
 				emu.getSh4Executor()->Stop();
+#endif
 #ifdef LIBRETRO
 			retro_rend_present();
 #endif
